      players: 'Three to twelve players; four or more is standard.',
      deck: '36 cards (standard); 30, 32, 33 or 35 depending on player count.',
      equipment: '36 cards (standard); 30, 32, 33 or 35 depending on player count.',
      dealing: "All cards distributed one at a time starting with the player to the left of the dealer. With 4, 6, 9 or 12 players use full 36-card deck; with 5 or 7 remove six of spades (35); with 8 remove all sixes (32); with 10 remove all sixes plus seven of spades and seven of clubs (30); with 11 remove sixes of spades, clubs and diamonds (33). Player to dealer's left is on the lead.",
    },
    turnFlow: "Each hand: deal all cards; then a bidding round (Pass, Solo, Solo in Hearts, Go Alone, Go Alone in Hearts) starting with the player on the lead. Each player bids once in turn; each must bid higher than the previous or pass. Winning bidder calls trump (Hearts automatic if bid was Solo in Hearts or Go Alone in Hearts) and, if not going alone, calls a card as partner; the holder of that card is the secret partner. Play: player to dealer's left leads. Players must follow suit if possible; if unable, must play a trump if able. No requirement to beat the card led. Winner of each trick leads the next. Solo team's trick points are combined; 61 or more wins the hand.",
